# render_0: Render Zero, FPS Tech's factory, the game's map, its title
# the map screen's. Metres, z up, degrees; x runs east and y north; the
# building's exterior is x 0 to 32 and y 0 to 24 with walls half a metre
# thick, drawn as the gaps between sectors. Four storeys in the plan
# views:
#
# ground (z 0): the factory floor, `bay`, 21 by 23 metres and 6 high
#   with two pillars, the spawn in its south-east corner facing the
#   mezzanine; `west_low`, the bay under the mezzanine along the west
#   wall, 2.7 high, open to the bay; the stairwell in the south-west
#   corner, `stair_ground` a T-shaped hall 6 high with the up flight
#   `up1` to `up6` (1.5 wide, half a metre a step) climbing north to
#   the mezzanine and the down flight `down1` to `down6` (2 wide)
#   descending north to the garage under a sloped ceiling, each an
#   enclosed shaft entered from the hall at its foot, since the hall's
#   one wall along a flight shares no edge with the steps and so makes
#   no portal; `door_stair` (tag 1) from the hall east
#   into the bay and `door_yard` (tag 2) from the bay east into the
#   yard, each 2.1 high.
# office (z 3): the mezzanine over `west_low`: `office_hall`, the
#   corridor the up flight arrives in, with `sill`, a metre-high
#   parapet along its east side whose window looks down onto the bay;
#   `office_a` and `office_b` west of it behind `door_a` (tag 4) and
#   `door_b` (tag 5); 2.8 high.
# garage (z -3): `garage` under the bay and the mezzanine, 2.6 high
#   with three pillars and parking stripes, reached by the down flight
#   and by the driveway through `garage_door` (tag 3) in its east wall.
# outside (z 0 and below): `yard`, fenced on the south, east, and
#   north, along the building's east wall with the door and a sign;
#   the driveway beside it behind `parapet`, a metre-high wall,
#   `drive_low` at the garage door and `drive_ramp` rising north at one
#   in four to the gate in the north fence; `beyond`, the street past
#   the fences, sky-walled at the world's edge. The sky is the ceiling
#   of every outside sector, 8 metres up.
#
# Five ambients, `floor`, `office`, `garage`, `yard`, and `stairwell`
# for the stair hall and both flights, by area; every door sector
# carries the ambient of the room it leads from.
# Three patrols of waypoints, tags 1 to 3: the bay, the garage, and
# the office corridor. Ten signs: the company's over the yard door and
# in the bay, the parking arrow on the facade, exits in the stair
# hall and by the yard door, the stairs beside their door, the bay's
# name on its north wall, a hazard on a pillar, the office's in the
# corridor, and the garage level by the down flight's foot.
